       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\n- **Ordered:** metformin 1700 mg PO TID, which is 5,100 mg/day.\n- **Maximum labeled dose:** 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, usually given as 850 mg TID. Extended-release is capped at 2,000 mg/day. Single doses are typically 500\u20131000 mg.\n- **Risk:** This is about twice the maximum daily dose. It raises the risk of severe GI toxicity and metformin-associated lactic acidosis, even with normal renal and hepatic function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- 850 mg PO TID with meals (2,550 mg/day)\n- 1,700 mg total per day, divided as 850 mg BID\n- 500 mg or 1,000 mg per dose at a different frequency\n\nIf you do want 1,700 mg TID, tell me and I'll enter it with a note documenting that it's intentional and exceeds the usual maximum. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
